  the log can be added behind it later in an hour. I'd rather give you the accurate version than stay consistent with
  my first answer.

  [1mPersistence — a decision I need from you[0m

  You deferred the team-vs-solo fork, which leaves v1's state in the air. In-memory-only means tasks vanish on refresh,
  which makes the app not really usable. My recommendation is [38;5;153mlocalStorage[39m behind a tiny [38;5;153msave[39m/[38;5;153mload[39m pair in one module.
  That is [1mnot[0m picking the solo path — it's a default adapter behind a seam, swappable for a server call when you decide.
  Roughly ten lines.

  [1mError handling[0m

  Small surface: reject empty/whitespace titles inline in the form, ignore clicks on already-removed tasks, and wrap the
  storage read in a try/catch so corrupt saved data starts you empty rather than white-screening.

  [1mTesting and tooling[0m

  Cheapest to set up before any code exists, so worth deciding now — this is the last question before I write the spec.

